course: dictionary
lesson: 12755
title: Duration: how long something lasts
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Duration is a noun. It means the length of time something lasts, from its start to its end. When you read about a film, a race or a holiday, the duration tells you how long it goes on. «The duration of the film was two hours.» So the film lasted two hours from start to finish.
explain: Duration is useful in maths too. If a race starts at 9:15 and finishes at 9:45, you find its duration by counting the time between the two. The duration is 30 minutes. Always count from the start to the end, not just the end time.
explain: You may also see the phrase «for the duration». It means for the whole time something lasts. «We will stay in the park for the duration of the picnic» means we stay until the picnic is finished. Look for clue words like start, end, long and short to spot duration in a sentence.
fact: Duration is a noun, and it means how long something lasts.
fact: The duration of something is the time between its start and its end.
fact: «For the duration» means for the whole time something lasts.
fact: In maths, a film from 3:00 to 4:30 has a duration of 1 hour 30 minutes.
fact: In music, a note's duration is how long the note is held.
exercise: «The duration of the film was two hours.» What does duration mean here? | *The length of time the film lasted | The number of people who watched the film | The start of the film | The picture on the screen
exercise: «The rain stopped after a short duration.» What does short duration tell you? | It was a long storm with thunder | It fell very hard all day | It was cold rain | *It lasted only a little time
exercise: The race started at 9:15 and finished at 9:45. What is its duration? | *30 minutes | 45 hours | 1 hour | 15 minutes
test: «We will stay in the park for the duration of the picnic.» What does for the duration mean? | Just before the picnic begins | *For the whole time the picnic lasts | Only for one minute at the start | Until we are tired and go home early
test: A film starts at 3:00 and ends at 4:30. What is its duration? | 1 hour | *1 hour 30 minutes | 3 hours 30 minutes | 30 minutes
exam: «The note was held for a long duration, so the music sounded full.» What does duration mean in this sentence? | How loud the note is | The highest note on the piano | *How long the note is held | The name of the note
